# Mobile queue row gesture contract

For rows on `LibraryQueueScreen`, keep one interaction contract:

- Tap the row to play it and remove it from queue.
- Remove is the swipe reveal action from `SwipeActionRow` only.
- Reorder is long-press drag on the row body, not a separate inline button.
- A decorative three-bar grip (`ReorderHandle`) sits in the row's far-right `trailing` slot
  inside `HomeFeedRow`. It marks that drag is available; it is not its own control. Taps and
  long-presses on the grip use the same play and reorder paths as the rest of the row.

These recognizers are composed deliberately:

- A quick tap reaches play-and-remove.
- Horizontal swipe reaches the remove reveal.
- Long-press vertical drag starts reorder and does not trigger play on release.

## Accessibility path

Drag gestures are not the screen-reader path. Queue rows remain `accessibilityRole="adjustable"`
with Move up / Move down actions (`misc.move_up` / `misc.move_down`) and those actions route through
the same reorder resolver as drag. The grip stays `accessible={false}` so it does not become a
separate focus target.

## Do not add parallel controls

- Do not add an inline remove button for queue rows.
- Do not add a More-menu remove row for queue rows.
- Do not add a separate play button that competes with row tap.
- Do not turn on `ReorderableSections` `showHandle` for queue rows — that places the grip outside
  the row press target. Keep `showHandle={false}` and render `ReorderHandle` via `HomeFeedRow`
  `trailing` instead.
- Do not wire a pan gesture to the grip alone; body long-press remains the drag activation.
